  "title": "High-DensityvSparsefNIRS_WordColorStroop_HD_Anderson_2025",
  "description": "This dataset contains high-density, multi-distance functional near-infrared spectroscopy (fNIRS) recordings collected while participants performed a word-color Stroop task. It was designed to compare high-density with sparse fNIRS measurement configurations for detecting task-related brain activity. The data are organized in BIDS format.",
  "methods_description": "High-density multi-distance fNIRS was used to acquire brain activity measurements during a Word-Color Stroop task. The study employed both high-density and sparse fNIRS configurations to compare detection sensitivity of brain activity.",
